["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>October water in the Interior is cold. A small boat tips fast. The cold, not swimming skill, is what kills.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The 1 10 1 principle for cold water. 1 minute of cold shock: gasping, get your breathing under control. About 10 minutes of useful movement: get out or onto the hull. About 1 hour before hypothermia makes you unconscious. Rough times, not exact.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold water: 1, 10, 1</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n  <g font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"56\" width=\"110\" height=\"170\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n    <text x=\"65\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\">1</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">minute</text>\n    <text x=\"65\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">Gasp.</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">Breathe.</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">Float in PFD</text>\n    <rect x=\"130\" y=\"56\" width=\"130\" height=\"170\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"195\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\">10</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">minutes</text>\n    <text x=\"195\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">Hands still</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">work: get out</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">or onto the hull</text>\n    <rect x=\"270\" y=\"56\" width=\"120\" height=\"170\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n    <text x=\"330\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\">1</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">hour</text>\n    <text x=\"330\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">Then</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\">hypothermia</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">knocks you out</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The first gasp kills: head under, you inhale water</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rough times. Water, body and clothing change them</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Use the 10 minutes for one job: get out, or onto the hull (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where 1 10 1 comes from</summary><ul><li>The \"1 10 1 principle\" is a name, not exact timing. It was made by physiologist Dr. Gordon Giesbrecht <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>1 minute:</strong> cold shock. You gasp and breathe hard. Get your breathing under control <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>10 minutes:</strong> of useful muscle movement before hands and arms stop working <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>1 hour:</strong> before hypothermia makes you unconscious <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Real times vary with water temperature, body and clothing. Some experts say it is too neat <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The first gasp is the killer. If your head is under water when you gasp, you inhale water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Tip: use the 10 minutes for one job: get out of the water or onto the hull. Do not swim for shore unless it is very close.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ZtAM5ZTn4k\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Cold Water Boot Camp - 1-10-1 Principle</b><small>Fall in cold water? 1 minute breathe, 10 minutes move, 1 hour.<br>SmartBoater, YouTube, 8 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"PFD stowed under the seat does not help: in cold water you will not get it on. PFD worn and zipped over your hunting jacket works. About 87 percent of boaters who drowned were not wearing one.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Worn, not stowed</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".25\"/>\n  <path d=\"M20 190 L180 190 L166 220 L34 220 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"70\" y=\"164\" width=\"60\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"176\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"110\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"86\" y=\"124\" width=\"28\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b6f48\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 60 l80 80 M140 60 l-80 80\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"6\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <path d=\"M220 190 L380 190 L366 220 L234 220 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"110\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"284\" y=\"124\" width=\"32\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b6f48\"/>\n  <rect x=\"280\" y=\"124\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"270\" y=\"168\" width=\"60\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"246\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Under the seat ✗</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"246\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">On and zipped ✓</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 87% who drowned wore none</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"PFD\">PFD</button> (personal flotation device) only works if you wear it. My lean: wear it, zipped, every minute.</li><li>Try it on over all your hunting layers.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the law says</summary><ul><li>Canadian law requires an approved PFD or lifejacket of the right size <strong>on board</strong> for each person <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>The law requires carrying it, not wearing it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. One exception: an inflatable PFD must be worn in an open boat <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. My lean: wear it, zipped, every minute on the water.</li><li>About 87% of boaters who drowned were not wearing one, per the Lifesaving Society <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Pick one that fits over your hunting jacket. Try it on with all layers before the trip.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Loading a small boat, seen from above. Read the capacity plate and count people, gear, guns and a deer. Heavy items low on the floor, centred side to side. Kayak: one person, guns cased and strapped, dry bag clipped in.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Load low and centred</text>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n  <path d=\"M30 120 Q 60 60 170 60 L240 60 L240 180 L170 180 Q 60 180 30 120 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"120\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"120\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"108\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n  <rect x=\"244\" y=\"104\" width=\"22\" height=\"32\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"206\" y=\"66\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"221\" y=\"81\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">kg</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"270\" y=\"82\">Capacity plate:</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"100\" font-weight=\"normal\">people, gear,</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"118\" font-weight=\"normal\">guns, a deer</text></g>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heavy gear on the floor, centred</text>\n  <!-- kayak -->\n  <path d=\"M40 254 Q 200 216 360 254 Q 200 292 40 254 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"254\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"236\" y=\"246\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"246\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"20\" y=\"226\">Kayak: one person</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"290\">Gun cased, strapped</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"290\">Dry bag</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Any motor, even a small electric: carry a PCOC (Pleasure Craft Operator Card) or other proof of competency (95 to 99%).</li><li>Never lean out for a bird. Bring it along the hull to the middle.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: boat, kayak and retrieving</summary><ul><li>Any boat fitted with a motor needs the operator to have proof of competency on board, usually a PCOC <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. The rule sets no minimum motor size, so a small electric counts <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>10 ft boat: check the capacity plate. Count you, your brother, gear, guns and a deer (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> plate numbers on your own boat).</li><li>Load low and in the middle. Heavy items on the floor, centred side to side.</li><li>Kayak: one person, guns cased and strapped, dry bag clipped in. Hard to shoot from and easy to tip.</li><li>No dog? Retrieve birds with the boat, motor off and gun unloaded, or with a long handled landing net (Tip).</li><li>Never lean out over the side to grab a bird. Bring it along the hull to the middle.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 320\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flowchart for guns in a boat in BC. Is the motor pushing the boat? Yes: every gun unloaded, no shooting. No, or no motor: a loaded gun is allowed while hunting or retrieving. For ducks and geese, also ask: is the boat still moving, even drifting from the motor? If yes, no hunting.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Guns in the boat</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"36\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#fff\">Motor pushing the boat?</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"110\" width=\"170\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"95\" y=\"136\" fill=\"#fff\">Yes: all guns</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"156\" fill=\"#fff\">unloaded, no shots</text>\n    <rect x=\"220\" y=\"110\" width=\"170\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"134\" fill=\"#fff\">No, or no motor:</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">loaded OK while hunting</text>\n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"196\" width=\"190\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#fff\">Ducks, geese: still</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">moving or drifting?</text>\n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"264\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#fff\">Yes: no</text>\n    <rect x=\"300\" y=\"264\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#fff\">Still: OK</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M150 80 L100 108\"/><path d=\"M250 80 L300 108\"/><path d=\"M305 170 V194\"/><path d=\"M260 240 L250 262\"/><path d=\"M330 240 L340 262\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Safest habit (Tip):</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">cased and unloaded</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">while moving. Shoot</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">from shore</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Motor pushing the boat: every gun <strong>unloaded</strong> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Ducks: no hunting from a moving motor boat <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact rules, BC and federal</summary><ul><li>BC <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"FVPA\">FVPA</button> (Firearm Violence Prevention Act), in force 1 October 2026, section 4: you must not transport, carry or store a <strong>loaded</strong> firearm in or on a vehicle or boat <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Section 5 of the same Act: no shooting \"in, on or from a vehicle or boat\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Hunting exemption, in force the same day: a loaded gun, and shooting, are allowed in a boat with no motor, or in a motor boat while the motor is not propelling it, when you are hunting or retrieving wildlife <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. For ducks and geese, the federal moving boat rule below also applies <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>So while the motor pushes the boat, every gun aboard is unloaded <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>BC synopsis, page 11, item 23 (2 October 2026 edition), deer and other game: no hunting from a boat unless it is <strong>not being propelled by a motor</strong>, or is held still in current, tide or wind by the motor <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Item 22: no hunting wildlife from a motor vehicle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Federal, ducks and geese: no hunting from a <strong>moving</strong> boat with a motor or sail. Drifting on momentum from the motor still counts as moving <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>BC synopsis, page 11, item 24 (2 October 2026 edition), ducks and geese: no hunting \"from or by using a moving boat that is equipped with a motor or sail\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Same as the federal rule. This replaced the old power boat rule on 1 October 2026 (99%, B.C. Reg. 66/2026).</li><li>Safe habit: gun unloaded and in a case while moving. Load only once you are stopped and set (Tip). Federal transport rules require a non restricted firearm to be unloaded, not cased <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Use the boat as a ride to a shore blind or a point. Shoot from land. It removes most of the legal and tipping risk.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a hunter stands in a small boat and fires. Recoil pushes him back, his high weight swings the boat over and it tips. Lesson: never stand to shoot. Sit square, feet flat.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why you never stand to shoot</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 200 200;0 200 200;-12 200 200;-60 200 200\" keyTimes=\"0;0.35;0.55;1\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M110 186 L290 186 L274 216 L126 216 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"96\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"156\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"156\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"186\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"156\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"186\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/>\n    <line x1=\"196\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"86\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8b10c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;0\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Recoil</text><path d=\"M120 150 h-60 m10 -6 l-10 6 l10 6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"236\" width=\"240\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sit square, feet flat</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One person moves at a time</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Recoil plus standing: over you go. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Sit square, feet flat. Shoot only inside your arc. One person moves at a time.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why boats tip</summary><ul><li>Small boats and canoes tip when weight goes high or to one side.</li><li>Recoil pushes you back. Standing turns that into a fall over the side.</li><li>Sit square, feet flat, shoot only inside your own arc. See the firearm safety session.</li><li>One person moves at a time. Everyone else sits still.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"5\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>If you go in</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 5</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capsize step 1: expect the gasp. Mouth closed if you can. Float in your PFD and get your breathing under control for about 1 minute.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Expect the gasp</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 q 25 -8 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"130\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"105.0\" y=\"144\" width=\"30\" height=\"34\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M150 110 q10 -10 20 0 q10 10 20 0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">1 min</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">gasp, then calm</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mouth closed. Float. Breathe for about 1 minute</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Expect the gasp. Float and breathe, about 1 minute.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capsize step 2: stay with the boat and hold on. It is bigger to see and helps you float. Do not swim for shore unless it is very close.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Stay with the boat</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 q 25 -8 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M170 150 Q 260 132 350 150 L344 170 L176 170 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" transform=\"rotate(180 260 156)\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"140\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"154\" width=\"30\" height=\"34\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M152 150 L176 150\" stroke=\"#d9b48f\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M90 90 l-50 0\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Not shore</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">It is bigger to see and helps you float</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Stay with the boat.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capsize step 3: climb onto the upturned hull to get as much of your body out of the water as you can.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Climb onto the hull</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 q 25 -8 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M150 150 Q 250 132 350 150 L344 170 L156 170 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" transform=\"rotate(180 250 156)\"/><g transform=\"rotate(-8 250 120)\"><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"118\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"212\" y=\"112\" width=\"70\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"116\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#5c5a4a\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Get as much of you out of the water as you can</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Climb onto the hull.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capsize step 4: if you cannot get out, use the HELP, Heat Escape Lessening Posture: arms crossed on your chest, knees up, ankles crossed.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Stuck in? HELP</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 q 25 -8 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"110\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"180.0\" y=\"124\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M184 140 L216 150 M216 140 L184 150\" stroke=\"#d9b48f\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M190 164 L176 190 L196 210 M210 164 L226 190 L206 210\" stroke=\"#5c5a4a\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">HELP: knees up, arms crossed</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Can't get out? HELP (Heat Escape Lessening Posture).</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capsize step 5: two people huddle, chests together. Once out of the water, stay out. Let the gun go, it is replaceable.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5. Two people? Huddle</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"150\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 q 25 -8 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0 t 50 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"116\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"165.0\" y=\"130\" width=\"30\" height=\"34\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"116\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"130\" width=\"30\" height=\"34\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M190 146 h20\" stroke=\"#d9b48f\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><text x=\"276\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Let the gun go.</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">It is replaceable</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chests together. Once out, stay out</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>5.</b> Two of you? Huddle. Let the gun go.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the steps in words</summary><ol><li>Expect the gasp. Mouth closed if you can. Float in your PFD and get breathing under control for about 1 minute <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Stay with the boat. It is bigger to see and helps you float <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Climb onto the hull to get as much of your body out of the water as you can <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Can't get out? Use the HELP (Heat Escape Lessening Posture): arms crossed on chest, knees up, ankles crossed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Two people? Huddle, chests together <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Once out, stay out. Water pulls heat away about 25 times faster than air <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Let the gun go. It is replaceable.</li></ol></details><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): The PFD in the bow locker is a cushion. The PFD on your chest is a lifejacket.</p></aside>","<aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>PFD under the seat \"to put on if we tip\".</li><li>Motoring after a crippled duck with a loaded gun.</li><li>Standing up to shoot or to pull in a bird.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Both wear PFDs over hunting layers. In shallow water, practise sitting back to back and reaching for a bird, gun unloaded.</p></aside><div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"ws-launch\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:0\"><span>Both PFDs on and zipped</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:1\"><span>PCOC on board if the motor is fitted</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:2\"><span>Guns unloaded and cased</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:3\"><span>Weight low and centred</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:4\"><span>Trip plan left with someone</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"ws-launch:5\"><span>Dry bag: spare warm layer, lighter, phone</span></label></div>","<ul><li>Boat and firearm rules read directly in federal and BC law (95 to 99%). Cold water and capsize lines: search previews (70 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.lifesavingsociety.com/water-safety/boating-and-lifejackets.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lifesaving Society, boating and lifejackets</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/medical-did-you-know/professor-popsicles-physiological-proof\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">McGill Office for Science and Society, Professor Popsicle (Giesbrecht, 1 10 1)</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordon_Giesbrecht\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gordon Giesbrecht, Wikipedia</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.coldwatersafety.org/1-10-1-myth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cold Water Safety: the 1 10 1 critique</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_escape_lessening_position\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Heat escape lessening position, Wikipedia</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/bills/billsprevious/1st42nd:gov04-3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firearm Violence Prevention Act, Bill 4, 2021, third reading text (BC Laws)</a>, sections 4 and 5, read directly. In force 1 October 2026 per the <a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/e4tlc21007\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">table of legislative changes</a>. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/168_90anif66_2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.C. Reg. 66/2026, Designation and Exemption Regulation amendments, effective 1 October 2026 (BC Laws)</a>, new sections 5.1, 18 and 19 (boat exemptions), read directly. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/190_84anif66_2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.C. Reg. 66/2026, Hunting Regulation amendments, effective 1 October 2026 (BC Laws)</a>, power boat definition repealed, new moving boat rule, read directly. Not yet in the consolidated regulation. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2022-105/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022 (Justice Laws)</a>, section 41, read directly, current to 21 September 2026. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, page 11, items 22 and 23, read directly. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-99-53/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Competency of Operators of Pleasure Craft Regulations (Justice Laws)</a>, sections 2 and 3, read directly, current to 21 September 2026. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2010-91/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Small Vessel Regulations (Justice Laws)</a>, sections 7, 10, 204 and 209, read directly, current to 21 September 2026. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-98-209/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Storage, Display, Transportation and Handling of Firearms by Individuals Regulations (Justice Laws)</a>, section 10, read directly, current to 21 September 2026. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>Note: boat and firearm rules now read directly in the federal and BC texts above. Cold water and capsize lines keep their own badges.</li></ul></details>"]